Z||000012||DaRkLoRD||05-10-2000||03:11 PM||||The scoop does help keep it cooler, in the Fiero the engine is cooled by air flowing into the bottom of the compartment and then out of the vents. By adding a new vent (in the form of a backwards scoop..) you allow one more place for the hot air to escape.<P>btw the Scoop article is also linked from Tom's website.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com/tom/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com/tom/</A> ||||reg||1
